{"agent":"recover-family","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"command":"roborev review --local --since 1bdefdf --sha 223d493 --agent kilo --model elmdeepseek/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash --reasoning medium","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"exit":0,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","note":"roborev via kilo on the LAN DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash reviewed the landed change (merge 223d493 vs first parent 1bdefdf: gates.py + tests/test_declared_reviewer_family.py), full review, 31 tool calls. It verified that gate record (CLI api/gates.py Evidence dataclass, MCP surfaces/mcp.py) cannot write the reviewer/family keys, so the declared family stays operator-controlled; ran the new tests plus the family/independence suites (86 passed); no correctness finding. One low finding: .strip().lower() is applied at the two call sites in reviewer_independence while family_of returns the raw map value (duplicate-then-drift hazard). Checked by me: reviewer_independence is the ONLY place that compares families (api/review.py, surfaces/commands/review.py and services/review.py only display or store them), so no input is wrong today; not filed as a bug, noted as a follow-up refactor. A refute-prompt run through the roborev daemon (job 850) sat queued behind jammed jobs and was cancelled. Supersedes the earlier same-family (Sonnet) rubber duck for independence.","output_bytes":111364,"output_digest":"a67dd66954f332c0","tail":"ow takes the family `ddflow review` recorded in gate evidence, trusting it only when the evidence carries a `reviewer` key (which the CLI/MCP `gate record` surfaces cannot write, since they build evidence from a fixed `Evidence` dataclass — verified in `ddflow/api/gates.py:302-317` and `ddflow/surfaces/mcp.py:229-263`). The check is now case-blind on both sides. The config commit disables `[worktree].local_files` because older ddflow rejects the unknown knob (`ddflow/config.py:1148` confirms the loader raises on unknown knobs), which is an intentional, documented workaround for B9cb7dd1c3b. Tests pass: the new file and the existing family/independence suites (86 passed).\\n\\nThe aggregate diff achieves the stated goal and the trust boundary in the new docstring is accurate as written for both agent-facing surfaces.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Severity: low** — `ddflow/services/gates.py:1232` and `ddflow/services/gates.py:1240`\\n\\nFamily normalisation (`.strip().lower()`) is now applied by hand at each comparison site while `family_of` (`ddflow/services/gates.py:1195`) still returns the raw map value. This is exactly the duplicate-then-drift shape the project has been bitten by: a future call site that compares `family_of(...)` output without repeating the normalisation would again treat `Alibaba` and `alibaba` as different families — the bug this series just fixed, reintroduced silently. Suggested fix: normalise once inside `family_of` (or have it return a canonical form) so no caller can forget.\\n\\n---\",\"time\":{\"start\":1790703463569,\"end\":1790703467422}}}\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1790703467545,\"sessionID\":\"ses_f11c5ca0effe3oCwgTHQ0aVjKL\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_0ee3e7ba5001221BaHiYLz1tf2\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"f4e114a7009525a634b9f9a9df223e71dbc6a131\",\"messageID\":\"msg_0ee3e594c001m43qsUM8UE40mT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_f11c5ca0effe3oCwgTHQ0aVjKL\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":65827,\"input\":64888,\"output\":437,\"reasoning\":502,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n\nrc=0\n","tree_sha":"d52d472ae784+95e0c70caf8cc336"},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":""},"id":"e5cb9a6755ff13fe39b99f8a0","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":3299,"schema":1,"subject":"B-fix-declared-family","ts":"2026-09-29T17:38:22.357256Z"}
